# Thoughts, items and tasks for the Server Room.
# Format is documented in src/defs.odin.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THOUGHTS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

:: thought harmonic_greed
NAME       The Harmonic Curve
PREMISE    The scoring is p over k times the sum of one-over-i. It means the
PREMISE    first person to solve a question takes the largest slice and every
PREMISE    solver after gets a thinner one. You keep turning it over. It is not
PREMISE    a scoring rule, it is a motive with an equation attached.
CONCLUSION You understand now what the curve is actually for. It does not
CONCLUSION reward being right. It rewards being right FIRST, and it punishes
CONCLUSION everyone who was merely right. Somebody in this building read that
CONCLUSION formula and saw an opportunity in it.
BEATS      5
RESEARCH   Logic -1
BONUS      Logic 2
BONUS      Visual Calculus 1

:: thought the_invigilator
NAME       The Man Who Was Supposed To Be Watching
PREMISE    There was a job. It had one requirement, which was to be present and
PREMISE    awake, and you have been unable to establish that you did either.
PREMISE    The thought sits behind your eyes and will not be looked at directly.
CONCLUSION You were supposed to be watching. You were not watching. Whatever
CONCLUSION happened here happened in the space you left. That is a fact about
CONCLUSION you and it is not going to stop being one, so you may as well pick
CONCLUSION it up and carry it usefully.
BEATS      7
RESEARCH   Volition -1
RESEARCH   Composure -1
BONUS      Volition 2
BONUS      Authority 1
BONUS      Empathy 1

:: thought cold_iron_stomach
NAME       Cold Iron Stomach
PREMISE    You have decided you are the sort of person who can look at a body
PREMISE    without flinching. You are testing the claim. It is going badly and
PREMISE    you are not stopping.
CONCLUSION You are not brave. You are just slow to react, and you have learned
CONCLUSION to present the delay as courage. It works well enough on other
CONCLUSION people, and tonight it worked on you.
BEATS      4
RESEARCH   Empathy -1
BONUS      Pain Threshold 2
BONUS      Half Light 1

:: thought the_second_cup
NAME       The Second Cup
PREMISE    Two people drank coffee in a room that was supposed to hold one.
PREMISE    You cannot stop assembling the second person out of the residue they
PREMISE    left: a rim mark, a chair angle, a door held open with a wedge.
CONCLUSION There is a way of reading a room where every object is a sentence
CONCLUSION somebody left unfinished. You have got the knack of it now, and you
CONCLUSION are not sure you will be able to switch it off afterwards.
BEATS      5
BONUS      Perception 2
BONUS      Shivers 1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ITEMS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

:: item headphones
NAME   Someone's Headphones
DESC   Over-ear, one cup worn through to the foam. Still faintly warm. There is
DESC   a sound in them if you hold them to your head, which you have done twice
DESC   now without deciding to.
EQUIP  yes
MOD    Perception 1
MOD    Shivers 1
MOD    Composure -1

:: item snapped_badge
NAME   A Snapped ID Badge
DESC   A staff access card, broken cleanly across the chip. The photograph is
DESC   intact. The name has been scraped, but not carefully, and not by
DESC   somebody who had much time.
EQUIP  yes
MOD    Authority 1
MOD    Interfacing 1

:: item hip_flask
NAME   Your Own Hip Flask
DESC   Empty. It has your initials on it, which is how you know they are your
DESC   initials. It was full at the start of the shift, and the shift is not
DESC   over.
EQUIP  yes
MOD    Electrochemistry 2
MOD    Volition -1

:: item wedge
NAME   A Rubber Door Wedge
DESC   Standard issue, grey, chewed at the thin end. It was under the fire door
DESC   and then it was not, and the person who moved it did so twice.
EQUIP  no

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TASKS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

:: task establish_self
TITLE  Work out who you are
DETAIL You woke on the floor of a server room with a name you cannot produce on
DETAIL demand. Start there. Everything else is downstream of it.

:: task check_the_contestant
TITLE  Find out what is wrong with the contestant
DETAIL She is face down on the desk and she has not moved. Establish, before
DETAIL anything else in this room, whether she is breathing.

:: task explain_the_freeze
TITLE  Explain why the scoreboard stopped at 02:14
DETAIL The board has not updated in three quarters of an hour. Nothing else in
DETAIL the building has stopped. Find out what is holding it.

:: task find_the_intruder
TITLE  Find who submitted the final flag
DETAIL The last flag was accepted eleven minutes ago from an account called
DETAIL guest_0, which was never registered and never logged in. Somebody put
DETAIL that row in by hand.

:: task name_them
TITLE  Say the name out loud
DETAIL You know who did it. Knowing is the easy half. The sysadmin is standing
DETAIL right there and is going to hear you either be right or be wrong.
